# Copy to orchestrator/.env (never in git). Only what the stack needs to start lives here; Tarik's secrets and
# per-cabinet settings live in Vault, read at start and every 5 minutes.

# The stack's own Postgres. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 24
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# The Experio server every cabinet is on.
ODOO_URL=

# ---- In Vault, not here ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# secret/tarik/orchestrator, this stack's own:
#   MODEL_API_KEY      the model's key (MiniMax-M3, at its Anthropic-style endpoint)
#   MODEL_API_URL      optional, the provider's address (default https://api.minimax.io/anthropic)
#   MAIL_BY_ORCHESTRATOR  the cabinets whose mailbox this stack answers, comma-separated (never one the n8n
#                      stack still answers)
#
# secret/tarik/shared, the same for every cabinet:
#   IMAP_HOST, IMAP_PORT (993), IMAP_FOLDER (INBOX), SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT (465 = SSL, 587 = STARTTLS)
#   MAIL_CERT_SHA256   the mail server's certificate fingerprint when it is self-signed (empty: usual check)
#
# secret/tarik/cabinets/<cabinet's exact Experio database>, one per cabinet (the cabinets are these paths):
#   ODOO_UID, ODOO_USER, ODOO_PASSWORD (or ODOO_API_KEY)  Tarik's user in that cabinet: a login
#                      returning another uid (wrong cabinet) fails every call
#   DRY_RUN            1 (default): read and report only, nothing posted to Experio
#   IMAP_USER, IMAP_PASSWORD, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASSWORD, SMTP_FROM  the cabinet's own mailbox
#   MAIL_MANAGER       told when a sender Tarik refuses writes to them (fallback to Experio's Responsable)
#   MAIL_ALLOWED_RECIPIENTS  who may receive Tarik's emails: addresses, @domain, patterns with *; empty = nobody
#
# The n8n stack's own keys in the same paths (AGENT_ID, N8N_MCP_API_TOKEN, MAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET) are ignored here.
